  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>The universe said to slow down, and stop. But your feet pressed on, faster and more determined.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Base attack bonus +3 or monk level 3rd, nonlawful.</p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> You ignore the effects of difficult terrain while moving. Whenever you take a move action to move and move through difficult terrain, you increase each of your movement speeds by +10 until the end of your next turn (and may benefit from the increased movement speed immediately).</p>\n<p>Whenever you make an attack action, a target struck by your attack must make a Will save (DC 10 + 1/2 your character level + your Wisdom modifier) or treat all movement they make as moving through difficult terrain for 1 round. This is a mind-affecting effect. A creature that successfully saves against this effect cannot be affected for 24 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Special:</strong> If you are a martial practitioner and can maintain martial focus (using the <em>Spheres of Might</em> system), you may use your practitioner modifier instead of your Wisdom modifier when determining the effects of Hubris Style.</p>\n<p><sup><strong>Source:</strong> Diamond Classes: Disciple of Chaos</sup></p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/general-feats#toc39\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
